{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789247615,"nonce":"kaLWfYRcnFgxomPr7CwLqDL+K/s=","title":"caribou-wren: bring a hosted wren_lift cycle to the cost of its own Immix","message":"Under WLIFT_GC_STRESS=1 on binary_trees (tiered, release) a hosted cycle\ncosts about twice wren_lift's own, and plain binary_trees runs about half\nagain as long in wall time with the same output and object counts.\n\nKnown levers, in the adapter and the core: mark_allocation re-enters the\nGC lock per object during wren_lift's mark (hold it across the mark phase\ninstead); collect_end does two side-table lookups per pinned object; the\ncore's drop_dead_traced walks every quantum of every traced block each\ncycle even though the adapter's descriptor has no drop hook; the anchor's\ntrace re-checks every pin. Also the per-object cost of the scheme itself:\na 16-byte prefix and an 8-byte pin per live object, and a lock hold plus a\npush per allocation.\n\nMeasure each lever separately on binary_trees and delta_blue before\nchanging the scheme.","files":null}]}